= Research Methods and Methodological Competence

#course(
  name: [Research Methods in Sport Science],
  id: [XS043007],
  semester: [2025–2026, Semester 1],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Research design in sport science
    - Literature research methods
    - Observation methods
    - Survey research methods
    - Experimental research methods
    - Organization and analysis of research data
    - Academic research and thesis writing
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces fundamental research methods used in sport science. It develops students' understanding of research design and the procedures involved in conducting scientific research. The course covers literature research, observation, survey research and experimental methods, together with the organization and analysis of research data. It also introduces the principles and procedures of academic research and thesis writing, providing methodological preparation for conducting and presenting research in sport-related fields.
  ],
)

= Sport Management, Industry and Organizations

#course(
  name: [Sport Management],
  id: [XS042009],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Foundations of sport management
    - Sport management methods
    - Sport management systems
    - Management of school sport
    - Management of competitive sport
    - Management of sport for all
    - Sport event risk management
    - Sport industry management
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces the fundamental principles, methods and functions of sport management and examines regularities in sport management activities. It develops students' ability to apply sport management theory to practical management problems. Major areas include sport management systems, school sport, competitive sport, sport for all, sport event risk management and sport industry management.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Introduction to Sport Industry],
  id: [XS042007],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Fundamental theories of the sport industry
    - Development of the sport industry in China and internationally
    - Sport markets and sport consumption
    - Professional sport
    - Intangible assets in sport
    - Sport venue management and operation
    - Olympic marketing
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces the basic theories and operating principles of the sport industry. It examines the development of the sport industry in China and internationally, sport markets and consumption, professional sport, intangible sport assets, sport venue management and operation, and Olympic marketing. Students learn to understand and apply fundamental sport industry principles in sport business and management practice.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Construction and Management of Social Organizations in Sports],
  id: [XS042006],
  semester: [2025–2026, Semester 1],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Concepts, types, characteristics and functions of sport social organizations
    - Historical development of sport social organizations
    - Internal governance and government support
    - Construction and management of different forms of sport organizations
    - Overview of sport nonprofit organizations abroad
  ],
  description: [
    This course examines sport social organizations from the perspective of their historical development and contemporary operation. Students study their concepts, types, characteristics and functions, as well as internal governance and government support. The course also addresses the construction and management of different forms of sport organizations and introduces sport nonprofit organizations in other countries.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Operation and Management of Fitness Clubs],
  id: [XS042010],
  semester: [2025–2026, Semester 1],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Principles and methods of fitness club operation and management
    - Operating models of fitness clubs in China and abroad
    - Management theories applied to fitness clubs
    - Current operational issues in the fitness club sector
    - Development trends in fitness club management
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces the content, methods and guiding principles of fitness club operation and management. It examines operating models and management theories used by fitness clubs in China and abroad, together with current operational issues and development trends. The course develops basic practical competencies for managing and operating fitness clubs.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Introduction to Sport Tourism],
  id: [XS042011],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Sport tourism as a field of study
    - Tourist subjects, tourist objects and tourism media
    - Relationships among the core elements of tourism
    - Historical evolution of sport tourism
    - Contemporary development of sport tourism
    - Fundamental patterns of sport tourism development
  ],
  description: [
    This course provides an overview of sport tourism by examining tourism activities and the relationships among tourists, tourism resources and tourism media. It introduces the historical evolution and contemporary development of sport tourism and explores fundamental patterns underlying its development, enabling students to develop a broad understanding of sport tourism as both a social phenomenon and a field of study.
  ],
)

= Sport, Society and Community

#course(
  name: [Sport Sociology],
  id: [XS042008],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Historical development of sport sociology
    - Sport as a social and cultural phenomenon
    - Relationships between sport and other areas of society
    - Social groups and social organizations in sport
    - Sport associations and community sport
    - Sport participation among different population groups
    - Social issues in sport from a critical sociological perspective
  ],
  description: [
    This course examines sport as a social and cultural phenomenon from a sociological perspective. It introduces the historical development of sport sociology and analyzes relationships between sport and other areas of society. Students apply sociological concepts concerning social groups and organizations to sport associations, community sport and participation among different population groups, and examine social issues in sport from a critical sociological perspective.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Community Sports],
  id: [XS042005],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [36],
  content: [
    - Concepts and theories of communities and community sport
    - Historical development of community sport
    - Community sport work and practice
    - Development of community sport in China and abroad
    - Community sport management and guidance
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces the conceptual and theoretical foundations of communities and community sport. It examines the historical development of community sport, the theory and processes of community sport work, and developments in China and abroad. The course develops students' competencies in community sport management and guidance.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Guide to Social Sports],
  id: [XS042004],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [32],
  content: [
    - Concepts and theoretical foundations of social sport
    - Status and functions of social sport
    - Institutions involved in social sport
    - Forms of social sport
    - Participation in social sport
    - Management of social sport
  ],
  description: [
    This course provides a broad and systematic introduction to social sport. It examines its conceptual system, social position and functions, relevant institutions and organizational forms, as well as participation and management. Students develop a foundational understanding of the theories and methods used in social sport.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Introduction to Social Sports Instructor],
  id: [XS042003],
  credit: [2],
  hours: [32],
  content: [
    - Concept and role of social sports instructors
    - Social responsibilities of social sports instructors
    - Management systems for social sports instructors
    - Professional standards and occupational norms
    - Policies and regulations related to social sports instructors
    - Basic methods of social sport management and guidance
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces the professional role and conceptual framework of social sports instructors. It covers their social responsibilities, management systems, professional standards, occupational norms, and relevant policies and regulations. Students develop basic methods and competencies for social sport management and guidance.
  ],
)

= Sport Science Foundations

#course(
  name: [Sport Anatomy],
  id: [XS042001],
  credit: [4],
  hours: [64],
  content: [
    - Morphological structure and functions of human organ systems
    - Developmental characteristics of the human body
    - Anatomical principles of human movement
    - Effects of physical exercise on human morphology and structure
    - Application of anatomical knowledge to exercise and fitness
  ],
  description: [
    This course introduces the morphology, structure and functions of human organ systems and their developmental characteristics. Students study anatomical principles underlying human movement and the effects of physical exercise on body structure, developing a theoretical foundation for subsequent sport science courses and for the application of anatomical knowledge in fitness guidance and services.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Sport Physiology],
  id: [XS042002],
  credit: [4],
  hours: [72],
  content: [
    - Human exercise capacity
    - Physiological responses to exercise
    - Physiological adaptation to exercise
    - Mechanisms through which exercise influences bodily functions
    - Physiological principles and methods of fitness exercise
    - Basic experimental skills in exercise physiology
  ],
  description: [
    This course examines human exercise capacity and physiological responses and adaptations to physical activity. It explains the mechanisms through which exercise influences bodily functions and introduces physiological principles and methods relevant to fitness. Through a combination of theory, experiment and practice, students acquire foundational knowledge and basic experimental skills in exercise physiology.
  ],
)

#course(
  name: [Fundamentals of Outdoor Sports],
  id: [XS042012],
  credit: [4],
  hours: [72],
  content: [
    - Fundamental knowledge and skills in outdoor sports
    - Planning and practical implementation of basic outdoor sport activities
    - Development and operation of outdoor sport projects
    - Outdoor first aid and safety
    - Instruction, management and organization of outdoor sport activities
  ],
  description: [
    This course develops foundational knowledge and practical skills in outdoor sports. It covers the planning and implementation of basic outdoor sport activities, the development of project-specific skills, outdoor first aid and safety, and the instruction, management and organization of outdoor sport activities.
  ],
)

